    "rationale": "PCSK1 encodes prohormone convertase 1/3, a serine endoprotease required to process multiple prohormones and proneuropeptides. Severe biallelic loss can cause congenital malabsorptive diarrhea that improves with age, followed by hyperphagia and obesity; impaired proinsulin processing produces a high proinsulin-to-insulin ratio. Strongest alternative resolved: POMC deficiency can cause hyperphagic obesity and adrenal dysfunction, but it does not account for severe congenital malabsorptive diarrhea, a high proinsulin-to-insulin ratio, and directly reduced PC1/3 expression; those findings specifically identify PCSK1 deficiency."
